---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="MyBackHaul — how it works">
  <main class="guide">
    <p><a class="back" href="/">← MyBackHaul</a></p>
    <h1>How MyBackHaul works</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      MyBackHaul matches distributors' loads with hauliers who have spare capacity on the way back — with a
      proof of delivery you can rely on, captured even where there's no signal.
    </p>

    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>
      Open the <a href="/app">driver app</a> and sign in with your email and password, or with Google. If your
      account belongs to more than one company, an <strong>Acting as</strong> switcher lets you choose which
      one you're working as — the screen changes to match.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img src="/guide/sign-in.png" alt="The MyBackHaul sign-in screen with email, password, and Continue with Google" />
    </figure>

    <h2>For shippers — post a load</h2>
    <p>
      Fill in where the goods are collected and delivered, the consignment (description, weight, pallets), the
      price, and the collection and delivery dates. Post it, and hauliers can see it straight away. MyBackHaul
      geocodes the route automatically within a minute.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img src="/guide/post-a-load.png" alt="The Post a load form with collection, delivery, consignment, and price fields" />
    </figure>

    <h2>For carriers — find a backhaul</h2>
    <p>
      Browse the available loads — each shows the route, pallets, headline price, and distance. Accepting one
      makes it your current job. You never see a shipper's private details until you've accepted.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img src="/guide/available-loads.png" alt="The Available loads browse showing loads with route, pallets, price, and an Accept button" />
    </figure>

    <h2>For drivers — the 30-second moment</h2>
    <p>
      When you've delivered, tap <strong>Mark delivered</strong>: take a photo of the goods, capture the
      recipient's name and signature, and record it. It saves to your phone instantly — <strong>even with no
      signal</strong> — and sends itself automatically the moment you're back online. You don't need to wait on
      the screen.
    </p>
    <div class="pair">
      <figure>
        <img src="/guide/mark-delivered.png" alt="The Mark delivered screen with photo, recipient name, and signature fields" />
        <figcaption>Capture the proof of delivery.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/guide/delivery-recorded.png" alt="The Delivery recorded confirmation — saved to this device, sent when you have signal" />
        <figcaption>Saved on your device, sent when you have signal.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <h2>Works with no signal</h2>
    <p>
      Deliveries happen in loading bays and rural lay-bys where signal is patchy. MyBackHaul is built for that:
      a proof of delivery is recorded on your device the moment it happens, and delivered to the shipper when
      signal returns — nothing is ever lost.
    </p>

    <p class="cta-row"><a class="cta" href="/app">Open the driver app</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
